#: docs/user-guide/studio/system-projects.md:17
msgid "one component's own design, in its own names; its port-backed relationships carry _provides_ / _parameter_ in their header (a _requires_ port has no formula, so it reads _declared_); its own behavior regions"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/studio/system-projects.md:17
msgid "_Editing AdaptiveLamp · used by 3 instances — its promise is what instances see; edits here reach every instance._ with **‹ System**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/studio/system-projects.md:19
msgid "Open a component's source by double-clicking an instance, or with **Edit Source** on an instance or component. Return with _‹ System_ or the inspector's **Back to System**. Simulate and Deploy always work on the whole system, whichever canvas is open."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/studio/system-projects.md:24
msgid "Instance nodes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/studio/system-projects.md:31
msgid "An instance node has the instance's name in a tinted header; one row per port — _requires_ ports and _parameters_ on the left, with a hollow socket while nothing is bound to them, _provides_ ports on the right; and in the body the component's name with its timing parameters, each shown with the system domain the instance gave it. A top-level relationship bound to a provided port shows the binding in its formula line: _= adaptiveLamp.brightness_."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/studio/system-projects.md:38
msgid "Socket colours are the concepts the ports carry _in the system_: a shared concept's own hue, or the instance's private hue for a private concept — so two instances of one component have two colours for their private _Brightness_. A red mark on the component's name means the source no longer keeps its promise."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/studio/system-projects.md:45
msgid "_A component's source: its own canvas, with the ports marked, and the bar that leads back to the system._"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/studio/system-projects.md:48
msgid "Gestures added on the system canvas"
